# CODEOWNERS - example governance map for the GH-600 control plane.
#
# CODEOWNERS turns "who must review sensitive files" into a rule GitHub enforces.
# Pair it with a branch protection rule that requires code-owner review, and an
# autonomous agent can never merge a change to a protected path on its own: the
# named owner (a human team) must approve first.
#
# Replace these example handles with real GitHub teams in your organisation.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
*                       @CertyPro/maintainers

# The control plane itself is the most sensitive area: workflows decide what
# agents are allowed to run. Require platform owners to review any change here.
/.github/               @CertyPro/platform-owners
/.github/workflows/     @CertyPro/platform-owners

# Agent automation logic governs routing and approval decisions.
/src/automation/        @CertyPro/platform-owners @CertyPro/maintainers

# Dependency manifests are a supply-chain risk surface.
/package.json           @CertyPro/platform-owners
/package-lock.json      @CertyPro/platform-owners

# Documentation can be owned by a docs team.
/docs/                  @CertyPro/docs-team
